<TimeSeries title="Lecture summaries" description="One-page summaries of the fifteen lectures: the economic question, the central relation, an individual problem with a worked answer, a consequential failure, and its repair.">
<div class="ea-narrow"><header class="ea-page-intro"><p class="ea-kicker">Fifteen lectures</p><h1>Lecture summaries</h1><p class="ea-lead">Each summary restates a lecture's economic question and central relation, poses one individual problem with a worked answer, and names a consequential failure with its repair. The chapter supplies the full argument, derivations, and laboratory.</p></header><div class="ea-prose"><p>Read the chapter first, attempt its assignment on the practice page, and run its laboratory in one language. Then use the summary to check that you can state the central relation, the failure, and the repair without the chapter open. The dates follow a model fifteen-week calendar for planning a semester.</p><ol>{lectures.map(l=><li><a href={`/time-series/lectures/${l.slug}/`}>{l.title}</a> · model calendar, {l.date}<br/><a href={`/time-series/${l.slug}/`}>Complete chapter</a> · <a href={`/time-series/code/#lecture-${String(l.order).padStart(2,'0')}`}>R, Julia, and Python</a></li>)}</ol><p><a href="/time-series/practice/">Assignments and worked practice</a> · <a href="/time-series/projects/">Project specifications</a></p></div></div>
</TimeSeries>
